WEBVTT

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.020
How long will we keep that man around?

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:43.540
When I visit Kikuya-san, I plan to rub his nose in it.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.630
We’ll be relying on our friend there.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:51.400
What were you thinking when you hired that man?

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:55.540
I was returning a favor to a vassal who helped me out once.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.960
I swear, you never learn.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.420
I already knew you were an expert at untying yourself.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.120
Now keep still.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.100
Wait.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.100
Don’t you think that’s enough?

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.930
I’ll take things from here.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.810
You’re a strange one.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.560
Did you tie the ropes securely yesterday?

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.880
We didn’t even need three guards in the first place.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:35.990
Did your master...

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.390
...reserve doubts about you all?

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.580
Please put that away.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.770
If we’re dismissed because of a quarrel,

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:55.820
I will, once again, find myself jobless.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.510
An unreliable guy like you would have been fired in a second.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.580
Now tie him up right.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.400
Please have faith in me, Matsukichi-dono.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:20.040
No, there’s probably no use in relying upon me.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.370
However, this time...

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.740
...I will come to help you tonight.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:30.810
Coming to Help

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.990
Did you spot the kifudas?

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.790
No, I didn’t because I did not search for them.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.500
Rescuing you is the first priority.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.400
If I give them reason to suspect me, all would be lost.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.000
So the master of this place has left?

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.230
He went with his guard to make a visit.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.750
In that case, I need you to look for the kifudas.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:22.510
I will return on my own.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:26.480
It will be impossible for you with that body.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.970
I will transport you to Ume-dono’s place.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.070
How pathetic.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.030
I’m always being rescued.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.680
How pathetic.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:56.960
Your occasional failures will never be used against you.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:02.930
The fact that no one thinks you’re pathetic is evidence of that.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.800
You are not pathetic.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.040
If anything, they think you are a little rash.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.590
Rash, huh?

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.010
That’s for certain.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.240
Okinu, lay out the futon on the second floor.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.450
Okay!

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.860
I will return to Ootsuya.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.640
I will act in a way so as not to draw suspicion.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.710
Was I also being rash on this occasion?

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:45.050
People act rash because there are things making them become that way.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:49.220
Like my comrades from the Five Leaves who mean a lot to me.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:55.810
From the Five Leaves.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.880
You look haggard. Lie down.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:16.050
What happened to your kid?

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.900
Living with the mother.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.880
And the father, the three of them.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.840
I couldn’t become the father.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.970
I couldn’t stop my evil ways even if I had a child.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:36.000
The family life disgusted me, being who I am.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:41.410
I couldn’t stand being a doting parent, always at hand.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:46.660
I think you’re admirable.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.290
Masa, what is it?

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.300
I couldn’t enter Ootsuya because an officer was there.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:03.820
When I went to Kikuya’s master to inform him of your safety, he wanted to see you.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.010
Lord...

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.970
Matsukichi-san?

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.890
I couldn’t retrieve the kifudas.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.340
That is all right.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.670
I’m glad you’re okay.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.570
I’ll wash the clothes.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.030
You’ll make the porridge.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:30.560
I’m glad Matsu-san is safe.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:32.750
Mm-hmm.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:38.040
There was a report that a thief broke into this place.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.980
Are you sure there’s no damage to claim?

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.630
Yes, none.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.230
The granary is also untouched?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.580
This is strange. Is it a lie?

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:52.940
How’s it look?

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.600
It looks to be nonsense.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.700
You’ll need to make a full report to the master.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.590
I’ll be going back.

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:00.060
Okay.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:05.020
It looks like Ootsuya-san is being investigated by the city.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:09.010
He might have handed the kifudas to an official.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:13.030
If that’s the case, this issue might be brought to light.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:16.290
That means this issue might be settled then.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:21.100
If it comes to light, then my inexcusable deed will also be exposed.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.250
But that was...

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:30.070
Even if it was all Ootsuya-san’s doing,
I still lost those kifudas entrusted to me.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:35.260
If that becomes common knowledge and he does not take responsibility...

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:41.000
I will get the kifudas back.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.600
What if we do an exchange?

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:47.570
That will be proper.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.700
I apologize.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.320
I should have searched when I had the chance.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.530
I need to go...

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.210
You’ll be exposed if you make a wrong move.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.000
You’re not one to get worked up.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.480
But for you to make that move despite your personality...

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.460
Matsu-san? Here’s some porridge.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.100
Eat this and rest for a while.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:18.610
You have some fine companions, Matsukichi-san.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:22.390
Though they may be both good and evil.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.370
That must be puzzling!

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.040
Lord...

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:31.810
Don’t worry. I won’t tell the others.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:50.230
Tavern

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.420
Good morning, Ichi-san.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.880
There’s someone I need to find.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:00.900
Okay.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.330
So are you feeling all right?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:10.310
I’d never have thought a ronin would go through all that trouble, and it annoys me to no end.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:13.010
But I owe him now.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:17.230
He does take some dealing with, sad to say.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.270
Masa.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:24.110
These are...

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:26.680
I got these from him.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.290
How?

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:32.870
So were you able to rescue him?

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:38.050
Thanks to you. Still, you have to answer for recommending me...

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:43.460
As long as the captive escaped, I felt obligated to do it.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.550
Well, everything turned out perfectly.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.620
The master must be relieved now.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:01.160
I will owe you for this.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:05.120
And the repaying of your debt with dirty money?

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:08.160
The lord doesn’t seem to mind.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.660
The money from the Five Leaves is not being used to erase the debt.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.620
So I’m wrong?

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:16.700
The money I get from jewelry is money that I earn.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.920
The lord knows that much.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:22.590
So what is the money from the Five Leaves for...? Ah.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.700
I strayed into forbidden territory again.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.720
The money I steal from the rich is used for drinks and my amusement.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:34.240
Anything that’s left, I give as offerings.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:40.430
I work for the Five Leaves to erase my debt to Ichi-san.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:43.190
You are very honest, Matsukichi-dono.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.850
I’ve said something out of bounds again.

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:53.120
Masa...

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.950
It’s the one I saw the other day that you said was for sale.

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:58.500
It’s not for sale.

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:03.400
It’s something I’ve kept without selling to anyone.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:05.410
Take it.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.600
Wait...

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:11.470
It’s fine. Send it to your sister back home.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.750
It doesn’t seem like they’re investigating anything.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:38.290
Hmm...

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.050
Something funny happened with that Yagi fellow last month.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:45.800
He’s a top-ranked officer of the Northern Magisterial District.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:48.730
He’s shrewd, but he seems like a man you can’t figure out.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.350
So is he the adopted son of the House of Yagi?

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:54.260
Is that right?

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:57.390
I think I heard something along those lines.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.700
Go check into that.

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:15.200
My lady, has the woman named Otake returned yet?

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:18.460
Let’s go to an inn already.

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.700
I will wait here.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:25.020
If I do not meet the one called Otake, I will not know where he is.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.130
Still...

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.590
Please go to an inn, Tasuke.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.090
Come on.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:35.890
Since she seems to take to the bottle, I’ll go check the pubs in this area.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:37.050
Please do.

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:43.470
Where in the world are you, Brother?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:56.990
Matsukichi-dono.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.450
Ume-dono has washed your clothes for you.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:05.410
Do you know of someone named Yagi who lives in this town?

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.850
Yes, in a way.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:14.400
I feel there is something about that man.

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.670
You’re really a handful.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:21.640
You get dragged around by an officer while running off at the mouth without a care.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:30.860
Still, Matsukichi-dono, Yagi-dono was the one who got me the guard job and who retrieved the kifudas.

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:34.860
Yagi-dono might very well be a benefactor.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:42.240
I probably shouldn’t have said anything.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:56.800
Sachi!

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:59.240
What are you doing in Edo?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:05.080
Brother, what were you doing that kept you from Nagaya?

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.190
I was guarding an estate.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.820
I came running here to Edo with my friend Tasuke.

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.820
Brother Bunnosuke is planning to marry me off.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:18.500
An arranged marriage?

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:22.250
Isn’t Chuujirou your childhood friend?

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.390
Yes.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:26.500
I cannot go along with what Brother Bun wishes for me.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:30.210
Still, you cannot avoid it by staying in Edo.

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:32.070
It’s better to return.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.210
I will not return.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:35.010
No, you will return.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:36.990
I hate you, Brother Masa!

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:37.670
Sachi!

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:41.440
I will not have you causing trouble for everybody!

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:48.580
I will go to the inn to tell Tasuke I met you.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:57.400
Now I’m seeing how resolute you can be.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.580
You really are an older brother.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:06.620
My lady, where are we going?

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.950
There’s something that is troubling me.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:23.080
Where did Brother go?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.640
Katsuraya.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.880
He is serving as a guard there.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.380
What is this Katsuraya?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.700
A house of ill repute.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:32.690
Huh?

00:16:32.690 --> 00:16:34.670
Now then...

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.000
Thanks for breakfast.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.000
What is it?

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:01.540
Bean Soup

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:08.580
I knew you were going to follow me for something.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:12.500
Are you worried that your brother found himself a woman?

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:17.940
Anyone would wonder since you two are living together in Nagaya.

00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:22.650
But since I’m mistaken, I feel a sense of relief...

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:25.660
...and a sense of disappointment.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.470
Disappointment?

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:32.860
At first, I thought your age and status were incompatible with Brother’s,

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:38.670
but now I feel that your beauty would be wasted on him.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:43.100
I’m not the woman that you make me out to be.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:48.210
Katsuraya

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:54.540
You’re going to be checking out the target for our next job.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:18:00.230
Are we clear, Masa? Don’t get close to that guy.

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:03.960
You mean Yagi-dono?

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:07.030
That’s right. Since he’s an officer.

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:10.550
Do you object?

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:14.000
No. I consent.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:21.590
I just don’t know what to do with you.

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:25.860
At the beginning, I didn’t know too much about you, but you seemed interesting.

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:29.060
Now it’s just getting irritating.

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:37.380
You gotta do something about that, Masa.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.170
Huh?

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.400
If that Hacchouborian were to suspect something and get that reaction from you...

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:47.590
You can’t fool anyone, so don’t meet him.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.430
I will be standing outside.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:09.070
So don’t let people see what you’re thinking, huh?

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:13.550
Still, you are good, Yaichi-dono.

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:16.500
I was quite startled by those words.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:29.230
You’re Tokujirou-san, right?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:34.260
You are a long-time friend of Soushi the Buddha.

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:40.490
There are a lot of rumors surrounding you.

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:44.750
What do you need?

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:49.590
The whereabouts of the one who sold out Kuhei’s crew of Bakuro to the city.

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:53.330
Would you happen to know?

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.520
Oh, Masa.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.870
What have you been doing since this morning?

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:11.430
I was asking people if they knew where Sachi is staying.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:14.940
If you mean Sacchan, she’s been right here since yesterday.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:15.980
Eh?

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:20.960
Sachi?

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:24.560
Otake-san, I brought you some tofu.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:27.780
Why are you here?

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:33.410
As a woman, I want to study her ways.

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:34.940
A woman like her?

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.050
So Brother, what do you seek?

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:38.030
Oh...

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:40.510
I want to give this to you.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:43.830
It’s from Matsukichi-dono.

00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:46.410
The jeweler?

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:49.110
Oh, my!

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.940
To be

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.940
continued

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:16.140
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:25.430
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:33.850
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:40.900
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:49.830
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:57.910
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:06.730
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:14.970
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:24.080
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:33.200
Next time on House of Five Leaves:

00:22:34.050 --> 00:22:35.020
I am Sachi.

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:37.810
Edo is so large, and it leaves me fatigued.

00:22:37.810 --> 00:22:41.530
There are a lot of girls wearing
gorgeous kimonos and having fun.

00:22:41.530 --> 00:22:43.790
It does leave me sort of envious.

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:46.330
A woman’s heart is complex.

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:48.010
Well then, the next episode’s title is:

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:49.970
“The Dirty Stray Cat.”
